    "body": "> add this pipeline to an enforced workflow or release-protocol step.\n\nFixed in published commit `d26b159fdf6fe32c8afa04be92ee0e335f35dc3c`. The required Windows canonical release job now runs `verify-stable-api-contracts` after canonical release succeeds and before the candidate upload. It passes the append-only current proof index and the exact candidate/attempt release-evidence path; a nonzero verifier result fails that required job.\n\nThe fix includes a portable, hash-bound packet with 2,340 entries and 4,722 aliases. The original `ad106d7e...da18` index remains unchanged. The live gate joins the current clean Git candidate and actual DLL/PDB/XML seal to the successor proof, while retaining historical runtime/compiler observations as historical evidence rather than claiming new executions.\n\nRetained local validation for this exact `d26b159` candidate: r6 canonical release passed all 14 commands and 10 checks, with 2,636 Release tests passed, 0 failed and 0 skipped. The actual r6-seal stable CLI exited 0 for 468 members and 3,744 dimensions; 17 focused tests passed, and independent increment review returned APPROVE with no blockers. These are local receipts, not a claim that the newly published hosted CI is green.\n\nThis completes the previously parked implementation gap. The earlier needs-human report remains a historical record; no human answer was fabricated to retire it. Exact-head hosted CI and PR settlement are tracked separately.",
